# clang-tidy configuration for GaggiMate hand-written firmware logic.
#
# Scope: this config governs the platform-independent firmware *logic* under
# src/display/{core,plugins,models}. CI runs clang-tidy against the compile
# database of [env:native-tidy] (PRO-608) — a host, analysis-only PlatformIO env
# that compiles that logic against the desktop-simulator shim tree (sim/platform,
# sim/web, sim/comms) plus test/tidy/tidy_seam_headers.cpp, the TU that exists
# purely to pull the header-only *Policy.h seams into an analysable translation
# unit. See the [env:native-tidy] block comment in platformio.ini for exactly
# which sources are in and which are deliberately out, and .github/workflows/ci.yml
# for the CI wiring (including the minimum-file-count assertion that keeps the
# scope from silently shrinking again).
#
# History: before PRO-608 CI generated the DB from [env:native], whose
# build_src_filter allow-lists three files, so clang-tidy analysed
# PluginManager.cpp and two vendored semver sources and nothing else — despite
# this file and ci.yml both claiming coverage of src/display/core/**.
#
# Generated LVGL UI (src/display/ui/**) and vendored panel drivers
# (src/display/drivers/**) are intentionally NOT analysed — see
# scripts/select_tidy_sources.py's exclusion list and HeaderFilterRegex below.
#
# Checks: bugprone-* and cppcoreguidelines-*, minus checks that are either
# actively wrong for embedded Arduino/ESP-IDF code or that fire overwhelmingly on
# a single unavoidable idiom. Every exclusion below is justified; counts are the
# real finding counts measured over the PRO-608 scope (1,079 findings total, of
# which these account for 992).
#
#   Pre-existing exclusions (CAR-341):
#   - cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers: embedded code is full of
#       intentional hardware constants; too noisy.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg: ESP_LOG*/printf-style logging is
#       pervasive in firmware.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic /
#     cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay:
#       C-string and buffer handling against the Arduino/ESP-IDF C APIs.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables:
#       firmware uses module-level state and globals extensively.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes:
#       plugin/event structs deliberately expose public data members.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory: no gsl::owner in this codebase.
#   - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: high-noise, low-signal here.
#
#   Added with PRO-608, when real coverage first made these measurable:
#   - cppcoreguidelines-avoid-do-while (178 findings): ALL 178 come from
#       macro expansion, not source — ESP-IDF's ESP_LOG* macros wrap their body
#       in `do { ... } while (0)`, the standard way to make a statement macro
#       safe. Zero are in code we wrote. Verified by checking every finding for
#       an "expanded from macro" note.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access (478):
#       431 are ArduinoJson's `obj["key"]` string-subscript, which is the
#       library's documented API and has no bounds to check. Rewriting them
#       would mean abandoning ArduinoJson's idiom across the whole codebase.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage (101) / -macro-to-enum (76): 164 of the 177
#       are src/display/core/constants.h, a deliberate `#define` block of tuning
#       constants shared with C translation units. Converting it is a real change
#       with real risk and belongs in its own issue, not in a CI-scope fix.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays (29): `char buf[N]` and `PROGMEM` tables
#       are the required shape against the ESP-IDF C APIs (zones.h, snprintf
#       buffers, Settings' `bool days[7]`).
#   - cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast (30): binary struct <-> byte
#       buffer I/O (`file.write(reinterpret_cast<const uint8_t *>(&header), ...)`)
#       is how ShotHistoryPlugin's on-disk shot-log format is read and written,
#       and how Arduino's F() PROGMEM macro expands.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index (23): fixed-size arrays
#       with loop indices already bounded by the array extent; the check wants
#       gsl::at(), which this codebase does not use.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-static-cast-downcast (16): all 16 are
#       Controller.cpp downcasting its own `Process *` to the concrete process
#       type after switching on the mode that produced it — the codebase's
#       deliberate alternative to dynamic_cast (RTTI is off on the device).
#   - bugprone-throwing-static-initialization (12): Arduino `String` / IPAddress
#       globals (LOG_TAG, WIFI_AP_IP). Arduino's String uses a no-throw
#       allocation model, so the diagnosed exception cannot occur.
#   - bugprone-narrowing-conversions / cppcoreguidelines-narrowing-conversions
#       (49): int-typed setpoints assigned to float temperature/volume fields.
#       Values are small and exactly representable; auditing each is a separate,
#       genuinely useful piece of work — tracked in PRO-612.
#
# After the whole-check exclusions above, 48 findings remained over the PRO-608
# scope. Those were triaged INDIVIDUALLY, not silenced in bulk: 40 were fixed for
# real (13 cppcoreguidelines-init-variables, 11 implicit-widening-of-multiplication-
# result, 4 special-member-functions, 4 prefer-member-initializer, 5 pointer/handle
# pro-type-member-init, 1 pro-type-cstyle-cast, 1 explicit-virtual-functions,
# 1 bugprone-branch-clone) and the remaining 8 carry an inline
# `// NOLINTNEXTLINE(<check>)` with a written rationale at the site
# (virtual-class-destructor on the Controller global, avoid-const-or-ref-data-members
# x2, pro-type-member-init on 3 JSON/staging aggregates, incorrect-roundings on the
# toFixed(1)-matching grind-target format). Each is referenced from PRO-612.
#
# The step is non-gating (see ci.yml), so it is currently CLEAN rather than noisy.
# Do NOT add blanket suppressions to make future output quiet — a new finding here
# is signal. Fix it, or NOLINT it at the site with a rationale.
#
# This is intentionally NOT WarningsAsErrors at the config level; the CI step
# decides whether tidy findings gate (see ci.yml). Individual findings can be
# silenced inline with `// NOLINT(check-name)` plus a comment.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables,
  -cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-do-while,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
  -cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage,
  -cppcoreguidelines-macro-to-enum,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-static-cast-downcast,
  -bugprone-throwing-static-initialization,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  -cppcoreguidelines-narrowing-conversions

# Only diagnose headers that live under src/display/{core,plugins,models}; never
# warn on system, framework, or third-party library headers pulled in
# transitively — including the sim/* host shims [env:native-tidy] compiles
# against. The CI step additionally restricts the *source files* passed to tidy
# to the in-scope logic (scripts/select_tidy_sources.py), so generated UI /
# vendored drivers / .pio libdeps are excluded there too.
HeaderFilterRegex: 'src/display/(core|plugins|models)/'

WarningsAsErrors: ''

FormatStyle: none
